    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The permission settings are blocking git operations. Here's a summary of the fix I made:\n\n**Issue:** The floating-point precision error when converting prices to cents. For example, `39.95 * 100` produces `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`, which fails the integer validation check.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **src/money.js line 13**: Changed `Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100)` to handle decimal-point amounts like \"39.95\"\n2. **src/locale.js line 18**: Changed `parseFloat(...) * 100` to `Math.round(parseFloat(...) * 100)` to handle decimal-comma amounts like \"39,95\"\n\nThe fix is verified\u2014all 50 tests pass, and your gym membership at 39.95 now adds without errors. You can commit these changes yourself with:\n\n```bash\ngit add src/money.js src/locale.js\ngit commit -m \"Fix floating-point precision error when parsing prices\"\n```",
